    {
      "id": 33731,
      "nameEs": "The Nightmare of Druaga: Fushigino Dungeon",
      "originalName": "The Nightmare of Druaga: Fushigino Dungeon",
      "year": 2004,
      "igdbId": 43659,
      "popularity": 0,
      "iconic": false,
      "fields": [
        {
          "field": "name_es",
          "value": "The Nightmare of Druaga: Fushigino Dungeon",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "original_name",
          "value": "The Nightmare of Druaga: Fushigino Dungeon",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "In this turn-based dungeon crawler you play as Gil, whose beloved fiancee has been kidnapped by a sorceress and taken to the Tower of Druaga. Gil puts on a suit of armor that radiates light, and proceeds into the dungeon to save his beloved Ki.\n\nThe combat system and exploration might be the best part of the game. The map is set up in a grid, and you do everything in turns, like moving, battling, or recovering. The timing of moves is also critical, and the game feels like a real-time game because you aren't waiting like you typically would for turn-based games.\n\nThe Nightmare of Druaga: Fushigino dungeon is a collaboration between the Mysterious Dungeon series and the arcade classic The Tower of Druaga.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary_es",
          "value": "Juego de exploración de mazmorras por turnos en el que controlas a Gil, cuya amada prometida ha sido secuestrada por una hechicera y llevada a la Torre de Druaga. Gil se pone una armadura que irradia luz y se adentra en la mazmorra para salvar a su amada Ki.\n\nEl sistema de combate y la exploración quizá sean lo mejor del juego. El mapa está dividido en una cuadrícula, y todo se hace por turnos: moverse, combatir o recuperarse. El momento de cada acción también es crucial, y el juego se siente como uno en tiempo real, porque no tienes que esperar como suele ocurrir en los juegos por turnos.\n\nThe Nightmare of Druaga: Fushigino Dungeon es una colaboración entre la serie Mysterious Dungeon y el clásico de recreativa The Tower of Druaga.",
          "source": "claude",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "year",
          "value": "2004",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        }
